Synthesis
  1. The scalar-ramp obstruction is exactly the shifted initial-segment equality case cell-by-cell.
  2. The S364 best non-scalar n=14 vector is not generic: it is scalar m=8 with one coordinate defect.
  3. Its 56 missed cells are the scalar cells uniquely blocked by the defect coordinate.
  4. No one- or two-coordinate scalar-neighborhood deformation is a non-scalar full blocker.
  5. The next finite proof target is a fragility theorem: every non-scalar deformation of a scalar ramp
     exposes at least one uniquely protected micro-staircase cell, then extend beyond small defect radius.
